// pfodWeb NOTE: excludes GPIO8-11 (LoRa SPI bus), GPIO12-14 (LoRa
// RST/BUSY/DIO0), GPIO17/18/21 (OLED I2C), GPIO36 (Vext power-gate) -
// see vendor pins_arduino.h.
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO0 tagged "button" - confirmed onboard PRG/USER
// button per Heltec official datasheet HTIT-WB32LA_V3 (Rev1.1), Pin
// description table ("GPIO0, connect to PRG switch") and Heltec
// schematic diagram (USER_SW S2, pulled up via R7 10K to VDD_3V3).
// Matches ESPHome device page (devices.esphome.io/devices/heltec-wifi-
// lora-32-v3/: "Function: Button, GPIO: GPIO0").
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO35 (pins_arduino.h LED_BUILTIN/LED alias) is
// vendor-confirmed as the onboard white LED (LED2), active-high, per
// Heltec official datasheet HTIT-WB32LA_V3 (Rev1.1) Pin description
// table ("GPIO35 ... LED Write Ctrl") and schematic (net "LED" through
// R19 330R to LED2 to GND); also matches ESPHome device page ("Function:
// LED, GPIO: GPIO35"). Deliberately left untagged/unexcluded here - it
// already has no chipGpios entry (excluded via the chip-level GPIO33-37
// octal-flash/PSRAM policy inherited from variants/esp32/esp32s3/
// board.json, same as sibling boards heltec_wifi_lora_32_V4,
// heltec_wireless_shell_v3, heltec_wireless_stick_lite_v3). Re-adding it
// would mean reversing a pre-existing chip-level pin exclusion, which is
// outside this task's scope - left for human review alongside those
// sibling boards' identical GPIO35 situation.
